#' undeRfactor: what one factor measures when the items come from two traits
#'
#' Functions for one-factor models fitted to items generated by two
#' correlated traits:
#'
#' * [phi_star()]: the trait correlation below which the one-factor solution
#'   stops being an equal composite and follows one trait (ML, ULS, WLSMV);
#' * [pop_fit()]: exact population discrepancy, fit indices, loadings and
#'   trait shares of the one-factor model, with every distinct minimum;
#' * [blind_spot()]: the trait correlations above which conventional cutoffs
#'   no longer reject the one-factor model;
#' * [factor_share()]: the share of each trait in a fitted factor;
#' * [order_check()]: whether item order or starting values change a
#'   one-factor solution in a sample.
#'
#' [two_trait_cor()] builds the population correlation matrix of a two-trait
#' design.
#' @keywords internal
"_PACKAGE"
